    "body": "# UC Berkeley — MEng\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#4 in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, Berkeley\n\nDegree route: MEng in EECS\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nFull-time EECS MEng completed in one academic year (Fall and Spring) with a technical concentration, engineering leadership coursework, and a team capstone. Concentrations include Data Science, Computer Systems, and Visual Computing among others.\n\nOrientation: Professional MEng · 1 year · Capstone · Leadership\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$73,767 — Academic-year tuition and mandatory fees (MEng nonresident, continuing); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nRegistrar Master of Engineering (All M.Eng Degrees) per-semester continuing totals: residents $29,767.75; nonresidents $36,883.25 (includes tuition, Student Services Fee, campus/transit fees, PDST $16,850 resident / $17,843 nonresident, NRST $6,122.50 for nonresidents, IREF, and health insurance $4,103). Program is Fall+Spring only → nonresident AY $73,766.50. New students add $119 document fee in first semester ($37,002.25 first-semester nonresident total).\n\nApplication timing: Apps open (Fall 2027 cycle open) · Deadline 6 Jan 2027 · 8:59 p.m. PST (MEng EECS). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMEng is a professional/industry program; do not assume PhD-style funding. Specific MEng fellowships not verified on fee pages fetched; unresolved beyond fee schedule.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Master of Engineering (MEng) EECS](https://eecs.berkeley.edu/academics/graduate/industry-programs/meng/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://registrar.berkeley.edu/tuition-fees/fee-schedule/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
