    "body": "# Columbia — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Columbia University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nColumbia CS MS: ≥30 points, designed for ~3 semesters, with breadth, PDL, and ≥6 points at 6000-level. Eight faculty pathways plus Personalized/Thesis by invite.\n\nOrientation: 30 points · Pathways · ~3 semesters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$67,728 — Academic-year tuition (SEAS MS, $2,822/point × 12 points × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nColumbia Engineering Graduate Tuition bulletin and SFS Graduate Engineering COA 2026–27: M.S. tuition $2,822 per credit/point. Full-time COA budgets 12 points/semester → $33,864/semester → $67,728 AY Fall+Spring. A typical 30-credit MS CS totals $84,660 in tuition across the degree (pace varies). Mandatory fees in the COA (health insurance, health service, university services, SEAS activities, document fee) and living costs are separate; CS is not listed with the IEOR/AI program fee.\n\nApplication timing: Fall priority 15 Jan · Fall final/regular 15 Feb 2027 (CVN year-labeled for Fall 2027) · Spring 15 Oct. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMS pathways page; department funding for MS not verified as guaranteed. Do not apply PhD funding.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS overview](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://sfs.columbia.edu/content/graduate-engineering-cost-attendance)\n- [SEAS graduate tuition bulletin](https://bulletin.columbia.edu/columbia-engineering/graduate-studies/graduate-tuition-fees-payments/)\n- [CS Admissions (MS deadlines table)](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/admissions8/)\n- [MS Program Application FAQ](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/appfaq/)\n- [CVN Computer Science Master's (Fall 2027 / Spring 2027 year-labeled)](https://cvn.columbia.edu/content/computer-science-masters-degree)\n- [MS requirements FAQ](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/regfaq/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
