    "title": "Duke — MS",
    "body": "# Duke — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#25 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Duke University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nDuke CS MS: 30 credits over three full-time semesters. Course-only, project, or thesis; optional AI/ML or Cybersecurity concentrations; master’s exam required.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · 3 semesters · Course/project/thesis\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$69,880 — Academic-year tuition (Graduate School master’s full-time × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nDuke Graduate School Tuition, Fees, and Ph.D. Stipend Schedule 2026–27: Master’s Students $34,940 per fall/spring semester → $69,880 AY. Summer I or II $17,470/term; after three full-time semesters, continuing/part-time $4,055 per unit. Master’s students must enroll full-time for at least three semesters. Mandatory fees (health, recreation, activity, student services; transcript fee first term) and health insurance are separate from the tuition figure. CS MS is 30 credits (coursework-only, thesis, or project).\n\nApplication timing: 1 Feb 2027 · 11:59:59 p.m. EST (MS Computer Science — Fall 2027). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nThe Graduate School’s CS MS page lists no financial aid available for the MS. External funding requires separate verification.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [M.S. in Computer Science program page](https://gradschool.duke.edu/academics/programs-degrees/computer-science-ms/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://gradschool.duke.edu/financial-support/tuition-fees-and-phd-stipend-schedule/)\n- [Cost to attend (master’s COA)](https://gradschool.duke.edu/financial-support/cost-attend/)\n- [Duke Graduate School application deadlines (Fall 2027 master's)](https://gradschool.duke.edu/admissions/application-deadlines/)\n- [MS requirements](https://cs.duke.edu/graduate/ms/ms-req)\n- [Master's options](https://cs.duke.edu/graduate/ms/course-options)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
