    "body": "# Georgia Tech — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#7 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Georgia Institute of Technology\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nCampus MSCS is 30 hours with one required specialization (11 areas; specialization coursework 15–18 hours). Course, Project (9h), or Thesis (12h) options. Complete within six years; keep distinct from OMSCS.\n\nOrientation: 30 hours · 1 specialization · Course / project / thesis\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$33,080 — Academic-year tuition (campus Master & PhD, out-of-country, 12+ hours × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nBursar 2026–27 Atlanta campus graduate Master & PhD Candidates: In-State $7,280/semester (12+ hrs) or $607/hr (1–11); Out-of-State $16,073/semester (12+) or $1,341/hr; Out-of-Country $16,540/semester (12+) or $1,379/hr. International-relevant figure uses Out-of-Country full-time: $16,540 × 2 = $33,080 AY. Mandatory student fees $608/semester at 4+ credits not included in the tuition figure. OMSCS ($227/hr) is excluded.\n\nApplication timing: 1 Feb 2027 · 11:59 p.m. ET (Atlanta campus MS CS — Fall 2027; not OMSCS). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nCampus MS funding not automatic; GRA/GTA pay reduced tuition per BOR policy when appointed. Do not apply PhD funding assumptions to MS.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MSCS specializations](https://www.cc.gatech.edu/ms-computer-science-specializations)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://bursar.gatech.edu/student/tuition/su27/su27_totals.pdf)\n- [Gatech Bursar Tuition & Fees](https://bursar.gatech.edu/tuition-fees)\n- [Fall 2026 Tuition and Fee Rates PDF](https://bursar.gatech.edu/sites/default/files/2026-07/fa26_totals_page_0.pdf)\n- [Graduate Costs (OSFA)](https://finaid.gatech.edu/costs/graduate-costs)\n- [GT GradApp program info (MS CS deadlines)](https://gradapp.gatech.edu/portal/program-info?cmd=view-program&program=86097380-be9a-4631-6407-50f3d959f466)\n- [MS CS admission requirements](https://www.cc.gatech.edu/ms-computer-science-admission-requirements)\n- [MS Computer Science program](https://www.cc.gatech.edu/degree-programs/master-science-computer-science)\n- [MSCS catalog](https://catalog.gatech.edu/programs/computer-science-ms/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
