    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/northwestern-cs.md",
    "title": "Northwestern — MS",
    "body": "# Northwestern — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Northwestern University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nNorthwestern CS MS: 12 graduate units, typically 3–4 quarters. Default course-only (Plan C); optional thesis (A) or project (B).\n\nOrientation: 12 units · 3–4 quarters · Course/thesis/project\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$70,986 — Academic-year tuition (TGS master’s full-time 3–4 units × 3 quarters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nNorthwestern Evanston Graduate Financial Aid / TGS Master’s COA 2026–27: full-time 3–4 credits/units $23,662 per quarter. Academic-year Fall+Winter+Spring = $70,986. Single unit $8,418; two units $16,836. Health Services Fee $298/quarter (F/W/S); NU-SHIP annual premium $5,996—fees not included in the tuition figure. MS Computer Science requires 12 graduate units (typically 3–4 quarters). McCormick SFS also lists $23,662/quarter full-time for several engineering master’s schedules.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 15 Sep 2026 · MS Fall 2027 staged: by 30 Nov · 31 Dec · 28 Feb · 15 Jun (portal may close when full). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CS Graduate Programs hub](https://www.mccormick.northwestern.edu/computer-science/academics/graduate/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (TGS master’s COA)](https://www.northwestern.edu/evanston-graduate-financial-aid/getting-started/tuition-cost-of-attendance/tgs/masters.html)\n- [McCormick graduate tuition](https://www.northwestern.edu/sfs/tuition/graduate/mccormick.html)\n- [CS Graduate Admissions (Fall 2027 open + MS staged dates)](https://www.mccormick.northwestern.edu/computer-science/academics/graduate/admissions/)\n- [TGS Application Deadlines](https://www.tgs.northwestern.edu/admission/application-procedures/application-deadlines.html)\n- [MS program](https://www.mccormick.northwestern.edu/computer-science/academics/graduate/masters/)\n- [Catalog CS MS](https://catalogs.northwestern.edu/tgs/computer-science/computer-science-ms/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
