    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/penn-cs.md",
    "title": "Penn — MS",
    "body": "# Penn — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#19 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Pennsylvania\n\nDegree route: MSE in Computer and Information Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nPenn CIS MSE: 10 course units with four constrained cores (theory + systems rules), CIS electives, and optional thesis (CIS 9990). Complete within seven years; min GPA 2.7.\n\nOrientation: 10 CUs · Constrained cores · Optional thesis\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$52,950 — Academic-year tuition (SEAS on-campus master’s, 3 CUs × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nPenn SRFS SEAS on-campus master’s 2026–27: tuition $8,825 per course unit (CU). Catalog CIS MSE requires 10 CUs; sample plans use 3 CUs in a typical Fall or Spring term → AY tuition reference $8,825 × 3 × 2 = $52,950. At 4 CUs/term: $35,300/semester ($70,600 AY). Mandatory fees at 3 CUs: General Fee $2,134 + Technology Fee $405 + Clinical Fee $385 (semester totals with tuition $29,399)—fees not included in the tuition figure. Full 10-CU degree tuition at $8,825 = $88,250. Online Engineering rates differ.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 15 Sep 2026 · Early 1 Nov 2026 · 11:59 p.m. EST · Regular 1 Feb 2027 · 11:59 p.m. EST (CIS MSE Fall 2027). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CIS MSE catalog](https://catalog.upenn.edu/graduate/programs/computer-information-science-mse/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://srfs.upenn.edu/costs-budgeting/seas)\n- [Residential master’s CS admissions](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/residential-masters/computer-science/)\n- [Penn Engineering How to Apply (Fall 2027 master's timeline)](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/how-to-apply/)\n- [Penn Engineering Master's Programs (CIS early deadline noted)](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/masters/)\n- [MSE in CIS requirements](https://www.cis.upenn.edu/mse-in-cis-requirements/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
