    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/rice-cs.md",
    "title": "Rice — MCS",
    "body": "# Rice — MCS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Rice University\n\nDegree route: Master of Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nRice MCS: 30-credit non-thesis professional master’s, normally 3 semesters, with specialization + internship + COMP 608.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · Non-thesis MCS · ~3 semesters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$66,784 — Academic-year tuition (Engineering master’s/PhD full-time × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nRice Bursar Engineering graduate rates 2026–27: Masters & PhD Full-Time Tuition $33,392/semester → $66,784 AY. Part-time approved $3,710 per credit (maximum $33,392/semester). MCS is a terminal non-thesis master’s requiring 30 credit hours (normally three semesters); catalog states MCS students are expected to pay full tuition with no university/department financial aid. GSA fee $45 AY, Student Organization $8, Health & Wellness Support $720 AY, and health insurance are separate. Online OMCS is a different per-credit schedule ($1,700/credit)—not used here.\n\nApplication timing: 10 Feb 2027 · Early scholarship consideration. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nThe on-campus program lists early scholarship consideration and limited TA/RA roles. Eligibility, amounts and international final deadline need confirmation; July 1 is labeled domestic.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MCS program home](https://cs.rice.edu/academics/graduate-programs/master-computer-science)\n- [Rank 27 cross-check](https://engineering.rice.edu/about/facts-rankings)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Bursar Engineering)](https://bursar.rice.edu/tuition_fee_rates/graduate-programs/engineering)\n- [GA Rice MCS](https://ga.rice.edu/programs-study/departments-programs/engineering/computer-science/computer-science-mcs/)\n- [MCS program](https://csweb.rice.edu/academics/graduate-programs/master-computer-science)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
