    "title": "UC Irvine — MS / MCS",
    "body": "# UC Irvine — MS / MCS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, Irvine\n\nDegree route: MS in CS / Master of Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCI research MS CS: ≥47 units with 4 core areas + electives; thesis or comprehensive exam. Distinct from the professional MCS (~15 months).\n\nOrientation: 47 units · Thesis or exam · ~2 years research MS\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$38,784 — Academic-year tuition and mandatory fees (graduate nonresident; research MSCS); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Prefer research MS; MCS labeled separately.\n\nUCI Registrar Graduate/Credential Student Fees 2026–27: Total Nonresident annual $38,784.44 (Tuition $13,722 + Student Services Fee $1,344 + campus fees + Student Health Insurance $7,771.86 + Nonresident Supplemental Tuition $15,102). California Resident annual $23,682.44 without NRST. Document Fee $87 new students only (not in annual total). Research Master of Science in Computer Science (MSCS) uses this academic graduate schedule. Separately, professional Master of Computer Science (MCS) cohort entering Fall 2026: Program Fee $63,500 total ($12,700/quarter × 5 quarters including Summer); first four quarters program-fee portion $50,800; registrar MCS schedule shows Total Fees Paid about $60,765.13 for Fall–Summer 2026–27 including campus fees and GSHIP—MCS is a different self-supporting schedule, not the primary research-MS figure.\n\nApplication timing: MCS international: 15 Jan 2027; MS not verified. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program comparison (MSCS vs MCS)](https://ics.uci.edu/academics/graduate-programs/program-comparison/)\n- [Professional MCS admissions FAQ](https://mcs.ics.uci.edu/faq/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (graduate fees)](https://reg.uci.edu/fees/2026-2027/graduate.html)\n- [MCS fee schedule PDF](https://www.reg.uci.edu/fees/2026-2027/compsci.pdf)\n- [Catalogue CS MS](https://catalogue.uci.edu/donaldbrenschoolofinformationandcomputersciences/departmentofcomputerscience/computerscience_ms/)\n- [MCS vs MSCS](https://mcs.ics.uci.edu/mcs-vs-mscs/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
