    "title": "UC San Diego — MS",
    "body": "# UC San Diego — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#12 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, San Diego\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science and Engineering\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCSD CSE MS offers Thesis, Comprehensive Standard, or Comprehensive Interdisciplinary plans with CS or Computer Engineering majors. Breadth (12 units) + Depth (12 units) plus electives/research; thesis needs 8–12 units CSE 298.\n\nOrientation: Thesis or comprehensive · Breadth + depth · ≥3 quarters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$38,087 — Academic-year registration fees total (graduate nonresident); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUCSD Graduate Registration Fees 2026–27: California Nonresidents annual total $38,087.17 (includes systemwide tuition $13,722, Student Services Fee $1,344, campus fees, mandatory health insurance $6,660, and Nonresident Supplemental Tuition $15,102). California Residents annual total $22,985.17. CSE MS uses the standard graduate schedule (not self-supporting). One-time Enrollment Services Fee $115 is included in the published Fall/annual nonresident total. International visa administration fee $200 is separate.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 2 Sep 2026 · Deadline 16 Dec 2026 · 11:59 p.m. PST (Fall 2027). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nCSE: financial opportunities page lists TA info; MS funding not guaranteed. Do not apply PhD funding policies.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS program](https://cse.ucsd.edu/graduate/degree-programs/ms-program)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://students.ucsd.edu/finances/fees/registration/2026-27/graduate.html)\n- [CSE Financial Opportunities](https://cse.ucsd.edu/graduate/financial-opportunities)\n- [CSE graduate admissions](https://cse.ucsd.edu/graduate/admissions)\n- [UCSD Grad application portal note](https://connect.grad.ucsd.edu/apply/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
