    "title": "UMass Amherst — MS",
    "body": "# UMass Amherst — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#25 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Massachusetts Amherst\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUMass Amherst CICS MS: 30 credits over ~2 years with four cores (Theory, Systems, ML + one) and ≥12 credits at 600+. Non-thesis; optional concentrations and Master's Project.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · 4 cores · ~2 years · Concentrations\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$35,613 — Academic-year tuition (graduate out-of-state/international, 9 credits × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUMass Amherst Bursar 2026–27 Graduate Tuition and Fees: Out-of-state & International at 9 credits tuition $17,806.50/semester → $35,613 AY (full-time threshold is 9+ credits; 12+ credits tuition $19,532.50/semester → $39,065 AY). In-state 9-credit tuition $8,083/semester ($16,166 AY). Campus fees on the bursar schedule (Graduate Service Fee, Graduate Health Fee, Senate Tax) and Student Health Insurance are separate from the tuition figure. Separately, Manning CICS publishes Total Tuition & Mandatory Fees Out-of-State/International $60,750 for the campus MS (program-level estimate including listed mandatory fees)—not used as the primary AY figure; prefer bursar. MS is 30 credits.\n\nApplication timing: Campus MS Fall: 15 Dec (month-day; year not labeled) · Online MS Fall: 1 Jun · Spring: 1 Oct. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CICS MS campus program](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/ms-computer-science-campus)\n- [Graduate program and rank 25 cross-check](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/masters)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Bursar)](https://www.umass.edu/bursar/tuition/graduate-tuition)\n- [CICS MS campus tuition page](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/ms-computer-science-campus/ms-campus-tuition-and-fees)\n- [UMass Grad School MS Computer Science (application deadlines)](https://www.umass.edu/graduate/academics/master-science-computer-science)\n- [CICS How to Apply — MS on campus](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/ms-computer-science-campus/how-apply-ms-program-campus)\n- [MS degree requirements](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/academic-policies/graduate-programs-policies/ms-degree-requirements)\n- [MS course requirements](https://www.cics.umass.edu/academics/academic-policies/graduate-programs-policies/ms-degree-requirements/ms-course-requirements)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
