    "body": "# UNC Chapel Hill — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUNC CS MS (Fall 2026+): 30 credits with four-category breadth, program product, technical writing, and comprehensive exam. Typically ≤4 semesters FT; 5-year limit.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · 4 breadth categories · ≤4 semesters FT\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$39,421 — Academic-year tuition (MSCS nonresident semester maximum × 2); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Cashier PDF notes rates not final until NC System Board of Governors approval.\n\nUNC Cashier Graduate and Professional Tuition and Fees Fall 2026–Spring 2027: Master of Science in Computer Science (mscs) Non-Resident $2,190.06 per credit hour, semester maximum $19,710.50 (9+ hours) → $39,421 AY Fall+Spring. NC Resident MSCS $1,153.56/credit, semester max $10,382. Campus-based mandatory fees $1,063/semester ($2,126 AY) not included in the tuition figure. Student health insurance is separate. Rates marked not final until Board of Governors approval.\n\nApplication timing: Final 9 Mar 2027 · Fellowship recommend 15 Dec 2026 · RA/TA recommend 5 Jan 2027 (MS/PhD Fall only). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Catalog CS GRAD](https://catalog.unc.edu/graduate/schools-departments/computer-science/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Cashier PDF)](https://cashier.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/259/2026/04/graduate-and-professional-tuition-and-fees-fall-2026-spring-2027.pdf)\n- [Graduate programs tuition hub](https://cashier.unc.edu/tuition-fees/graduate-programs/)\n- [CS Admissions Deadline (year-labeled fellowship/RA/final)](https://cs.unc.edu/graduate/graduate-admissions/admissions-deadline/)\n- [UNC Grad School Computer Science program sheet](https://gradschool.sites.unc.edu/computer-science/)\n- [MS requirements](https://cs.unc.edu/graduate/ms/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
