    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/washington-cs.md",
    "title": "Washington · Seattle — MS",
    "body": "# Washington · Seattle — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#7 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Washington\n\nDegree route: Professional Master’s Program in CSE\n\nApplication status: PMP: no F-1 / J-1 applicants\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUW Allen School: no general full-time terminal MS for most external applicants. Options are part-time Professional Master's (PMP, local/working professionals) or PhD with possible en-route MS.\n\nOrientation: Restricted · PMP part-time or PhD\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$17,130 — Typical academic-year instructional fees (PMP, 15 credits) — no F-1/J-1; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Availability: PMP does not support F-1 or J-1 student visas.\n\nUW Allen School PMP Costs & Fees: as of autumn 2026, per-credit instructional fee $1,142 (same rate regardless of residency/citizenship). Typical enrollment 4–5 credits/quarter (12–15 credits/year) → typical academic-year instructional cost $17,130 at 15 credits; typical program cost $45,680 at required 40 credits. About $295/quarter additional mandatory student fees. Eligibility: PMP does not support F-1 or J-1; international students need another status allowing Seattle-area residence and part-time study. Traditional research MS/PhD funding routes differ—this catalog id maps to the published PMP fee schedule with that visa restriction.\n\nApplication timing: PMP Autumn: 1 Jul (month-day; year not labeled) · Winter: 2 Nov 2026 (winter 2027 extension) · Spring: 1 Feb. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [PMP How to Apply (quarter deadlines)](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/pmp/admissions/how-apply/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (PMP costs)](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/pmp/program-overview/pmp-costs-fees/)\n- [PMP eligibility (no F-1/J-1)](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/pmp/admissions/requirements/)\n- [UW fee-based program rates PDF](https://finance.uw.edu/tuition-fees/files/docs/fee-programs/2026-27-fee-based-program-rates-5.7.2026.pdf)\n- [PMP admissions](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/pmp/admissions/)\n- [PMP overview](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/pmp/)\n- [PhD FAQ](https://www.cs.washington.edu/academics/graduate/phd-program/phd-admissions/faq/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
