    "body": "# Harvard Business School — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#4 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Harvard University\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nHBS MBA: 2 years. Year 1 Required Curriculum; Year 2 Elective Curriculum (30 credits). Case-method RC core listed on HBS site.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · RC then EC · Case method\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$84,760 — Academic-year tuition; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nNine-month, single-student budget: $130,318, excluding a $1,500 computer estimate. Summer housing and optional activities can add costs.\n\nApplication timing: Round Two · 5 Jan 2027 · 12:00 p.m. ET (Class of 2029 / matriculating fall 2027; R1 passed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nHBS need-based scholarships are open to admitted domestic and international students. Aid applications follow admission; personal eligibility and amount are assessed individually.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-004, SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-075, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MBA program](https://www.hbs.edu/mba)\n- [Tuition and attendance budget](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/financial-aid/tuition-assistance/cost-of-attendance)\n- [Curriculum](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/academic-experience/curriculum)\n- [Case method](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/academic-experience/the-case-method)\n- [Need-based scholarships](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/financial-aid/tuition-assistance)\n- [MBA application dates (Class of 2029)](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/admissions/application-dates)\n- [MBA admissions](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/admissions)\n- [Degree requirements](https://www.hbs.edu/mba/handbook/academic-information-and-policies/degree-requirements)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
