    "title": "Michigan Ross — MBA",
    "body": "# Michigan Ross — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#13 in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Michigan, Ann Arbor\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nRoss Full-Time MBA: 2 years, 57 credits. Prescribed Y1 core with MAP; Y2 electives; summer internship required.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 57 credits · MAP core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$83,946 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA, non-Michigan resident / international); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nMichigan Ross Full-Time MBA Tuition & Financial Aid: 2026–2027 rates approved by the Board of Regents in June 2026 — Non-Michigan Residents/International $83,946 per academic year; Michigan Residents $78,586. Mandatory fees $246.89 per full term; International Student Services Fee $500 per term for F/J visa students. Living-cost guidance (books, food & housing, personal, loan fees) is separate. 2027–2028 rates to be posted July 2027. Full-time MBA only — not Weekend/Online/EMBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 4 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. ET (Full-Time MBA; R1 passed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nMAP is a required seven-week consulting project preparing students for internships and careers. A project is not a guaranteed paid internship.\n\n## Funding\n\nAutomatic merit scholarship consideration on admission; $10,000 to full tuition. No separate application. Federal loans US-only; internationals use private loans. True Grit and several awards open to domestic and international students per affording page.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-006, SCH-007, SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-077, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program / academic source](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba/curriculum/map)\n- [Full-Time MBA Tuition & Financial Aid](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba/admissions/tuition-financial-aid)\n- [Full-Time MBA](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba)\n- [Affording Your MBA](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba/admissions/tuition-financial-aid/affording-your-mba)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions (deadlines)](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba/admissions)\n- [Full-time MBA curriculum](https://michiganross.umich.edu/graduate/full-time-mba/curriculum)\n- [Core course requirements](https://rossweb.bus.umich.edu/academics/curriculum/core-curriculum/full-time-mba/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
