    "title": "Washington Foster — MBA",
    "body": "# Washington Foster — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#20 in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Washington\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nFoster Full-Time MBA: 2 years, 88 credits. Integrated Y1 core; customized Y2 electives; summer internship/project.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 88 credits · Integrated core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$60,180 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA, nonresident; 3 quarters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUW Foster Full-Time MBA Tuition and Financing: Non-resident $20,060 tuition per quarter + $403 fees; Resident $14,166 tuition + $403 fees. Academic-year (three-quarter) nonresident tuition = 3 × $20,060 = $60,180 (tuition+fees AY ≈ $61,389). Published Total Estimated Program Cost (six quarters / two years) is $122,778 nonresident / $87,414 resident — full-program totals, not used as the annual tuition field. Cohort rate held for both years once enrolled. Full-time MBA only.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 5 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. PDT (Full-time MBA 2026–2027; R1 passed; final for internationals). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-047, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-time MBA curriculum](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/curriculum/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/tuition-and-fees/)\n- [Full-time MBA Admissions (2026–2027 deadlines)](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/admissions/)\n- [Full-time MBA](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/)\n- [Course descriptions](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/course-descriptions/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
