    "path": "03-business/programs/washu-mba.md",
    "title": "WashU Olin — MBA",
    "body": "# WashU Olin — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Washington University in St. Louis\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nOlin Full-Time MBA: 2 years, 67 credits (25 core + 42 electives). Optional specializations; electives can start in year 1.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 67 credits · Optional specializations\n\nFaculty and supervision: The specialization page identifies Patrick Moreton as faculty advisor for Strategy and Consulting. This is an advising role, not confirmation of research supervision availability.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$72,700 — Academic-year tuition (Olin Full-Time MBA; 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nWashU Olin Full-Time MBA Cost, Aid and Scholarships (posted Spring 2026) for candidates starting Fall 2026: Tuition $72,700 ($36,350/semester) under Academic Year 2026–27 — equals two flat-rate semesters. Program Fee $900, Student Government Fee $130, Health and Wellness Fee $350 per semester (fees not in the $72,700). Published Total $150,920 ($37,730/semester) is the four-semester / full-program estimate (4 × $36,350 tuition + 4 × $1,380 fees = $150,920), not used as the annual tuition field. Bulletin 2026–27 lists Full-Time MBA $36,350 per semester (four semesters standard). Page note calling the $72,700 'entire program' conflicts with semester math and bulletin; AY figure used. Full-time MBA only — not Flex/EMBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 7 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. CT (Full-Time MBA Fall 2027; R1 passed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-052, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Curriculum](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/curriculum.php)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/cost-aid-scholarships.php)\n- [Bulletin 2026–27 master's financial (PDF)](https://bulletin.wustl.edu/grad/business/graduate-masters/financial/financial.pdf)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/specializations.php)\n- [Full-Time MBA How to Apply (Fall 2027 deadlines)](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/apply.php)\n- [Full-Time MBA program](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/)\n- [Full-Time MBA](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/mbas/full-time-mba/index.php)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
